<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Finnish, a draft not yet read by a fluent reviewer (#495). The notes on each string are in values/strings.xml.
    The driver is addressed with the informal "sinä", as Finnish apps do. "Vehicle" is ajoneuvo, never a word for
    bus; "route" is linja; "run" is vuoro (a timetabled departure); "trip" is matka; "stop" is pysäkki;
    "block" is kierto; "report" is raportti, "reporting" raportointi; "agency" is liikennöitsijä; "dispatcher" is
    ajojärjestelijä; "fleet number" is kylkinumero; "diagnostics" is vianmääritystiedot.
    A placeholder takes no case ending, so the word beside it carries the case ("linjalla %1$s", "ajoneuvolla %1$s").
    A run's start time goes before vuoro with no "klo" ("6.58 vuoro"), since the phone formats the time.
-->
